From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:49:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: an address-less mailto: in an HTML message drafts in
 its chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bots like StickersBot put `mailto:?body=<command>` links in their HTML
messages: no address, because the reply goes to the bot. Upstream asks
which chat to draft the body in. When the link comes from a message, the
answer is that message's chat, so draft there directly; the user still
reviews and sends it, so a mail can prefill the composer of its own chat
and nothing more.

The HTML viewer's link relay now carries the message id next to the
account (`#open=…&acct=…&msg=…`, slothfulchat-web's html-email.ts and
runtime.ts), and __slothfulProcessQr takes it as an optional third
argument, routing such mailto: links to useOpenMailtoLink with it.
Links with an address keep the existing flow.
